 Sauron is  essentially a second tier villain in  Beren and lúthien the real threat in the  story is saurons boss a guy named  Morgoth the original Dark Lord in  Tolkien's mythology  he's a being so powerful that a massive  army of angels eventually has to invade  middle-earth to remove him from the  picture even Sauron is terrified of him  and with good reason as the ultimate  source of evil Morgoth was behind the  creation of dragons  orcs werewolves and trolls he  even boasts a personal bodyguard of  balrog x' each as powerful as the one  that killed Gandalf that one time  personal story  Tolkien's wife Edith was the inspiration  for the beautiful lúthien whose songs  enchant Morgoth and move even the  personification of death to tears Edith  meant Tolkien when he was just 16 his  guardian forbade him to see her but  within hours of turning 21 he proposed  and she accepted Tolkien later wrote to  his son Christopher that the love story  was first conceived in a small woodland  glade filled with hemlocks at Roos in  Yorkshire in those days Edith's hair was  raven her skin clear her eyes brighter  than you have seen them and she could  sing and dance the two were eventually  buried together sharing a simple  tombstone that bore the names Beren and  lúthien  badass heroine one of the common  criticisms of Lord of the Rings and The  Hobbit is that nearly all of the heroes  are men the book version of The Hobbit  famously doesn't have a single female  character a owen basically stands alone  in Lord of the Rings books although  Peter Jackson expanded our Irwin's role  for the movies while he invented toriel  out of thin air Beren and lúthien seems  like it's heading in the same direction  when Lu thien's father gives Baron a  quest to win his daughter's hand in  marriage in a subversion Baron and his  all-male band of companions fail  catastrophic Lee lúthien has to escape  from her father and personally faced  down Sauron to rescue her warrior and  distress from his 